  "instructions": [
    {
      "primary_message": "Place curry paste, oil, soy sauce, salt, and pepper in a medium bowl. Stir to combine the spice paste. ",
      "secondary_message": "2 tbsp Thai curry paste, red\ntoasted sesame oil\n⅛ tsp salt\n⅛ tsp black pepper"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Pat the cod dry with paper towels and place on a plate. Drizzle with half of the spice paste, then turn to coat the fish. (Reserve bowl with remaining spice paste for the salad.)",
      "secondary_message": "340 g cod fillet"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Preheat a skillet over medium-high heat.",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Once the skillet is hot, add oil and swirl to coat the bottom. Add cod and pan-fry until golden brown and cooked through, 3-4 minutes per side. Transfer to a clean plate. ",
      "secondary_message": "toasted sesame oil"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Meanwhile, wash and dry the fresh produce. ",
      "secondary_message": "½ lime\n½ English cucumber\n1 avocado"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Juice lime into the bowl with the remaining spice paste. Add honey and stir to combine the dressing. ",
      "secondary_message": "2 tsp honey"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Trim and halve cucumber lengthwise, then cut crosswise into thin half-moons. Add to the bowl with the dressing. ",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Halve and pit avocado; using a spoon, scoop out the flesh and small dice. Add to the bowl.",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Roughly chop cashews. Add to the bowl, along with the carrots, and stir to combine the salad. ",
      "secondary_message": "¼ cup cashews, roasted unsalted\n½ (283 g) bag shredded carrots"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "To serve, divide cod and salad between plates. Enjoy!",
      "secondary_message": null
    }
  ],
